I tend to find teleportitis to be not such a big deal (although I also
avoid it until I have at least a chance at TC). But if I happen to get
teleportitis before TC, the main thing to avoid is angering a
shopkeeper. Here's how I do it: Turn off autopickup; use the #chat
function to find prices in a shop, rather than picking the items up
(this is a good idea anyway, to avoid paying for certain scrolls that
can disintegrate); and if you want to buy something, pick it up and
pay for it on the next turn. The chances of teleporting out on that
turn are pretty slim, and if you teleport out while not carrying
anything, the shopkeeper won't care.
